{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Behold, of the fatness of the earth shall be your dwelling.</b> With this I can bless you, that your dwelling shall be in a fat land, with some subjugation to your brother — <b>and from the dew of the heavens above</b>." "<b>And by your sword you shall live.</b> And you shall live <b>from the dew of the heavens</b>, without needing the labor of the ground that requires rain, and you shall live also by your sword in warfare. And that you shall wage war to pursue <b>your brother</b> or another — this follows from <b>when you rebel</b>: that you shall cry out over the violence when <b>your brother</b> subjugates you beyond what is proper."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "Sforno reads תריד as deriving from ריד / רדה (to rule/subjugate); the phrase 'תצעק חמס על שישעבד אחיך בך יותר מן הראוי' is rendered hyper-literally as 'you shall cry out over the violence when your brother subjugates you beyond what is proper.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:05.751375207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}